<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">St Angelo Fort</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1505">1505</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Fort St Angelo, Kannur Fort</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">St Angelo Fort is a coastal fort at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannur">Kannur</a>, on the Malabar coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerala">Kerala</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, built by the first Portuguese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-de-almeida">Francisco de Almeida</a>, in 1505 with the permission of the Kolathiri ruler. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> captured it in 1663 and rebuilt it, then sold it to the Arakkal ruler Ali Raja in 1772. The British took it in 1790 and made it a military base, and it is now a protected monument.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/st-angelo-fort.jpg" alt="St Angelo Fort" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Frank Vincentz · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Malta_-_Birgu_-_Fort_Saint_Angelo_(Upper_Barrakka_Gardens)_01_ies.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
